ios-d2s fork for the Samsung Galaxy Note 10+ (d2s)

This repository combines original work with material from other projects. Each keeps its own
license. Not an exhaustive legal review.

- Apple XNU (xnu-8796) and Apple open-source components: APSL 2.0,
  https://opensource.apple.com/apsl/. The patches in xnu/patches/ are derivative works of XNU.
- Upstream ports this fork builds on: gorkemoji/ios-d2s, orhunnx/ios-a5xelte,
  dipa-studio/ios-sweet. They did not state an overall license at the time of writing (see
  README), so their original files are kept as published, with their authors credited.
- Code written after Linux drivers (for example shim/dreamlte/touch_probe.c): GPL-2.0, see the
  SPDX headers of each file.
- Mesa 3D (mesa-26.2.6), including the Panfrost Gallium driver: MIT and related permissive
  licenses, https://www.mesa3d.org/license.html. This repository holds only build scripts and
  patches (tools/d2s-gl); Mesa is fetched at build time from freedesktop.org.
- libdrm headers (tools/d2s-gl/libdrm): MIT.
- Ideas and public documentation consulted, with no code copied unless a file says so:
    * hakios, https://github.com/oosexgang/hakios-xnu-kernel (MIT, and APSL for XNU-derived files)
    * ios-sailfish, https://github.com/joranv1/ios-sailfish
    * UniXNU, https://github.com/UniXNU/UniXNU
  The Metal plug-in approach (a private-base subclass built at load time with a logged stub)
  follows hakios' HakiosMetal.m (MIT); tools/d2s-metal/D2SMetal.m is a rewrite for this device.
- Tools used at build time: blacktop/darwin-xnu-build, blacktop/ipsw, uniLoader and others;
  see the README credits.
